WEBVTT

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.200
What's important in order to live

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:13.490
Finding the lake was a big win for all of us.

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:19.060
But the sun was strong,
the humidity in the forest was high...

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:24.550
...and it was very hard making the three-hour round trip.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.810
What are you doing, Luna?
Get out of my way! I'm really thirsty!

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:12.460
Give me some more water.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:14.200
No, there isn't much left.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.660
We're going to gather more again today, right?

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.550
We have something we need to do before then.

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.650
What is this thing?

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:21.850
It's this.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.420
Isn't that the rubber boat?

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:28.600
It sure is.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:31.860
We're going to dig a big hole and fill it with this.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:35.290
I get it! We're going to store water in it, right?

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:36.570
Correct!

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:40.540
After that, we can stop goin' for water all the time.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.020
Don't spray sand on me!

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.940
Kaoru, lend me that.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:05.520
Don't get so smug.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:06.890
It's easier with my hands!

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:12.290
It's only soft on the surface!

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.410
Try to put up with it a little.

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:22.090
If you find something that seems useful, bring it back.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:23.890
--Thank you.
--Thank you.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:24.830
Where's mine?

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:26.930
There isn't one.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:29.540
Then hand that over!

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:31.980
I'm using this!

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:33.980
Stop that, Howard!

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.190
This one's way better! I'm saved!

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:54.850
Use it carefully.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:56.930
Why you...

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.780
Who do you think you're looking at when you say that?

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:02.820
Howard, you dig over there.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.000
Shut up!

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:06.080
And what's your deal?

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:07.900
You're not doing anything yourself.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.260
You're just giving orders like you're all that!

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.040
You may take it as selfish...

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:18.270
...but giving people the right directions
is my duty as the leader.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:19.860
You're the leader?

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:21.870
Who decided that?

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:25.680
This isn't just an extension of the school trip.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:27.380
Then what would you prefer we do?

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.590
Make me the leader.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.450
You?

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.160
The least suitable to be the leader...

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:37.510
...is the selfish, cowardly...

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:40.750
...type like you with no leadership skills.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.630
What?

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:44.390
Both of you, stop it!

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:45.360
Yeah.

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:50.500
Well then, we'll decide who's best suited for leader once we've looked at everyone's qualifications.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:51.780
Yeah.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:52.900
Agreed!

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:56.050
Kaoru, are you okay with that too?

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:56.930
Yeah.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:59.930
I guess it's decided.

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:03.700
Fine.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.760
We depart for the lake!

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:11.690
Be careful!

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:24.040
Halt!

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:27.660
A monster?

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.320
What's up with it scaring me like that?

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:47.740
It's so cute!

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:50.500
Hey, let's call that thing a 'Tobihane'.

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:51.740
Tobihane?

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:53.050
Yeah.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:56.030
(Tobihaneru: to hop)
Because of how it hops all over the place.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.000
Yeah, that sounds good.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:01.810
Once we've collected water, let's capture that tobihane.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:03.570
For a pet?

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:05.050
For food.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.540
It's been a while since we all came here together.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:23.460
Oh yeah!

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:26.460
Sharla, give this lake a name too.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:30.570
Let's see...

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.390
A lake of sprites.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:37.000
Fairy Lake! How's that?

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:40.110
Fairy Lake...

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.490
That's a good name.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:59.110
Luna!

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:01.710
Howard!

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.490
Don't play pranks on people!

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:14.630
What's wrong?

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:18.810
Luna?

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:21.040
I just...

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:24.640
Look!

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.220
There's fruit!

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:29.560
It's true!

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:33.270
There's fish too.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:35.260
What's wrong?

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:39.640
That's the tree you talked about, right Luna?

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:47.780
It's big, wide, and it gives you the
feeling that it will cradle you gently.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:50.610
Then what's that tree's name?

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:53.090
Let's see...

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:55.410
The Great Tree.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:57.640
The Great Tree...

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:01.300
I think that's a very good name.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:04.560
Sharla, you're like a poet.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:10.190
Hey, come to think of it, it would be great
if we could build a house at the top of that tree.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:12.830
That's obviously impossible.

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:15.270
Hey, let's go over to The Great Tree.

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:32.440
Look at this footprint!

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:34.150
This shape...

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:37.210
It's the same as the ones left around the shuttle.

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:43.560
Then the thing that attacked the shuttle
was that big animal we saw here before.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.570
You didn't realize it then?

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:48.810
It was a bad time for it just then.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:50.330
I see...

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:53.110
It may be a little dangerous to live here after all.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.860
There's a giant lizard, too!

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:59.710
But there's plenty of water and fruit...

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.570
Are you okay?

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:14.910
Be careful!

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:16.680
You spilled a little.

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:18.400
Sorry...

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:22.320
It's not like Shingo did it on purpose...

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:26.180
We all suffer from the mistake of any one.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:30.760
If it had all spilled out here,
we would have had to go back to the lake.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.640
I know. I'll be careful.

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:43.980
With this, we don't need
to worry about rationing the water.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.790
So you say, but I can't call it enough.

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:50.440
When you're thirsty, get my permission first.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:52.640
What do we do with these?

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.910
Everyone will take one plastic bottle.

00:10:57.530 --> 00:10:58.770
Take care of that much yourselves.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.570
We'll have the fruit for dinner.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:04.090
Just this isn't enough.

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:07.230
I'll go look for fruit with Sharla.

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:12.040
Then Kaoru, Shingo, and Bell, you take care of fishing.

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:14.220
Got it.

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:16.240
I'll get the tobihane.

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:20.180
After all, I'm the only one with hunting experience.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.710
I won't have anyone going around alone.

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:24.310
I'll accompany you.

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:26.730
Do what you want!

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:30.570
But if you're slowing me down, I'll leave you behind.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:42.140
In the end, all we got were
the mushrooms and fruit Luna and Sharla found.

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:44.070
Chako, check them out.

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:44.950
Okay!

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:55.040
No good! These're poisonous mushrooms!

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:56.310
These are?

00:11:56.930 --> 00:11:58.880
But they look so tasty...

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:02.130
You can't judge by appearances.

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:06.060
These're no good either.

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:07.260
Really...

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:08.580
That's disappointing.

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:15.310
So that means all we have to eat today
are the fruit we brought back from the lake?

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:18.510
Just that? I want to eat meat!

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:20.200
Meat...

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:25.340
I want to eat a big hamburger with a fried egg on it.

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:29.930
Or a thick juicy steak!

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:32.500
Or crispy fried bacon.

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:35.440
Or a carefully blended beef stew!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.640
Now I can't stop...

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:40.810
So only your imagination is mature.

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.700
What? You...

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:45.270
We have nothing but fruit.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:48.210
Tomorrow we'll definitely find food.

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:51.440
Meat, meat!

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:17.630
Oh no, oh no! Very bad!

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.690
It's prickly, puddly rain.

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:07.840
Where do you think you're going?

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:09.960
I'll look for food.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.740
We said everyone would wait inside.

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:15.630
I'll worry about myself.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.280
You're confused as to who the leader is.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:18.790
I won't approve of it.

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:24.530
This is great!

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:28.340
What does a leader do at a time like this?

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:31.230
Are you thinking of how you should punish Kaoru?

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:34.530
But there's no student council here.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:36.120
Miss Student Council President.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:38.260
Howard, give it a rest!

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:39.530
Shut up!

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:42.030
I'm irritable 'cuz I'm hungry!

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:47.260
I'm going out for a while as well.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:49.540
I'm not responsible if anything happens.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:56.580
Is that okay?

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:58.960
I warned him.

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:04.810
Maybe I should search for fruit too.

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:07.470
I won't go anywhere dangerous...

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:12.040
Do what you want.

00:15:17.990 --> 00:15:20.310
Sharla and I will go with Luna.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.000
It'll be safer with three.

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:23.820
Hey...

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:41.780
Bell.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:42.980
Hey.

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:44.310
How did it go...

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:45.940
..with the fruit?

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:48.590
I couldn't find any.

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.090
Really...

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:51.870
What's this pit?

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:53.370
I'm making a trap.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:54.720
A trap?

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:58.360
You mean, to catch a tobihane?

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:01.490
What will you do once you catch it?

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:05.290
Will you kill it?

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:07.320
Such a cute animal?

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.880
What kind of silliness are you spouting?

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:14.760
We didn't get anything today!

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:17.460
Whether it's a tobihane or the giant lizard...

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:20.090
...if we don't kill and eat it <i>we'll</i> die.

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:23.480
I agree with Howard's view.

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:24.960
But...

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:26.540
...I pity them.

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:30.610
But you're fine with what you buy
and eat from the supermarket.

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:34.260
That's right! It's just like Kaoru said!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:35.890
Wait!

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:40.770
I know what everyone's trying to say, but I think you should try to understand how Sharla feels.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:45.290
I mean, none of us have any
experience doing this in the past.

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:01.280
Howard! Hurry!

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:04.680
I haven't eaten in two days.

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:07.690
I don't have the strength left in me.

00:17:10.540 --> 00:17:12.270
Howard, what are you doing?

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:13.230
I'll leave you behind!

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:24.420
Sharla, that's amazing!

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:27.510
If we don't try hard and search even more...

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:29.610
The tobihane will get killed!

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:31.300
Sharla...

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:37.600
I guess in the end, it's just the fruit that you found, Sharla.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.100
Howard! It went that way!

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.690
I know!

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:01.390
Did you see that?

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:03.100
I chased him in!

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:04.660
How do you like that?

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:09.510
What's wrong?

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:12.660
We caught a tobihane.

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:14.610
It looks like it's in pain.

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:16.240
What are you doing?

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:18.210
Howard...

00:18:18.940 --> 00:18:19.730
...will you eat it?

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:21.960
I'll...

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:24.360
...well...

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:27.440
Menori, what do you plan to do?

00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:29.430
I'd...

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:32.110
Please, let it go!

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:33.610
It's hurt.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:36.250
If we let it go, it wouldn't live.

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:51.460
I'll do it.

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:52.600
Luna...

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:54.340
We...

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:58.360
...don't know how much longer we'll have to live here.

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:02.240
We can't run away from what we have to do to survive.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:08.990
I'll do it.

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:13.580
But...

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:18.740
Stop...

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:21.250
The poor thing!

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:46.540
You should eat.

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:50.460
I hate...

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:53.050
I hate you, Bell!

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:56.070
Sharla...

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:12.760
Understand his side.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:22.080
Sharla, you understand best of all
that Bell is really a kind person.

00:20:41.730 --> 00:20:43.080
Put more kindling on it.

00:20:50.710 --> 00:20:54.910
I know that Bell was only thinking
of everyone's well being.

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:56.050
But...

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:57.570
...but...

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:15.590
I'm sorry for speaking without thinking.

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:17.930
No...

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:20.730
I'm sorry, Bell.

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:24.590
I know I did something I shouldn't have.

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:28.080
But I want you to forgive me, just this once.

00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:32.070
I know.

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:40.730
Hey, this is about the leader,
but the most appropriate out of all of us...

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:42.100
...is Bell, don't you guys think?

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:47.860
Bell knows best what's important
in order to live on this island.

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:49.510
It's impossible for me.

00:21:50.050 --> 00:21:50.670
But...

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:52.960
I think it should be Luna.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:54.460
Me?

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:59.110
No way, no way! I don't have any
leadership ability, and I'm a scatterbrain.

00:21:59.350 --> 00:22:00.940
But you have compassion.

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:03.810
I'd agree to Luna as well.

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:05.690
I agree too.

00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:07.470
Kaoru, what do you think?

00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:09.490
Fine by me.

00:22:10.170 --> 00:22:11.710
I said, it's impossible!

00:22:12.530 --> 00:22:14.710
What're you sayin'? Accept it!

00:22:15.400 --> 00:22:17.390
Menori, Howard, what do you think?

00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:22.690
If four people agree out of seven,
it's a decision by majority.

00:22:23.710 --> 00:22:26.160
It can't be helped! I guess it's fine.

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:29.880
Then we're agreed that the new leader is Luna!

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:31.300
Good luck, Luna.

00:22:34.680 --> 00:22:37.940
If everyone's so sure of me,
I guess I'll give it my best.

00:22:38.260 --> 00:22:39.120
That's the spirit!

00:23:03.550 --> 00:23:07.490
Everyone has trouble waking up, and is weary
and irritated from sleeping in the small shuttle.

00:23:08.180 --> 00:23:12.530
It looks like we have no choice but
to build a waterfront house by the lake.

00:23:13.680 --> 00:23:16.230
And there's piles of water 'n food there, too.

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:23.950
Chako surveys, Shingo draws up the blueprints,
and everyone helps cut down trees, but...

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:28.230
Next time: We can definitely live together amicably.
